// Read from the inventory: Ateula's copy of the Noviodunum hostage roll.
@speaker Hostage roll
=== start
~ set roll_read
Two tablets in a small, neat, Roman hand. People by people: Lingones four, Senones six, Treveri three, Bituriges five, Cadurci of Brigodunon three, a dozen more peoples, nearly a hundred names. The writing is Latin, but Ateula has written each Gallic name the way it should sound.

Beside some of the names, in the right-hand column, a few words: a merchant's name, a sum, "half paid." There are a great many of them. The Cadurci of Brigodunon are not the only children in Gaul who have been sold forward.

At the bottom, smaller, a line that isn't part of any roll: "Let them decide with their eyes open."
* Put it away. -> END
